// Computation kernel
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

// computation kernel
//
// Optimizations compared to the baseline:
//  - Use row-wise accumulators tmp_acc and y_acc held in registers instead of
//    repeatedly loading and storing tmp[i] / y[i] inside the inner j-loop.
//    This removes two loads and two stores per iteration of j.
//  - Access x through the same state used for A and B (x[s]) instead of
//    rebuilding a separate state for every j. The extra 'i' index present in
//    the state is ignored by x’s structure, which only depends on 'j'.
//  - Keep the traversal order (i outer, j inner) to preserve the original
//    row-major streaming access pattern for A and B.
//
// A tunable constant is provided for potential future blocking in 'j' if
// architecture-specific tuning is desired. Currently we rely on the natural
// row-major layout for good cache behavior and on the compiler for
// vectorization of the inner accumulate loop.
